  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There seems to be some differences in the avatar bundling process for build and test, vs build and publish for avatars in sdk3. Specifically, it looks like build and test only compiles and bundles the necessary shader variants for the avatar in question, where as build and publish seems to be compiling and bundling all possible variables, heavily bloating avatar size. This behavior is still observed in the latest sdk VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2021.01.19.18.17.\nBuild & Test:\n 2.7 mb     10.7% Assets/Silent's Cel Shading Shader/Shaders/Crosstone (No Outline).shader\n 2.3 mb     9.1% Assets/Silent's Cel Shading Shader/Shaders/Crosstone.shader\n 186.2 kb     1.1% Assets/Toon/Shader/Toon_ShadingGradeMap_TransClipping.shader\n 185.0 kb     1.1% Assets/Toon/Shader/Toon_ShadingGradeMap.shader\n 2.5 mb     28.5% Assets/_PoiyomiShaders/Shaders/Toon/S_Transparent_PTTO.shader\nBuild & Publish:\n 11.0 mb     27.0% Assets/Silent's Cel Shading Shader/Shaders/Crosstone (No Outline).shader\n 9.3 mb      22.8% Assets/Silent's Cel Shading Shader/Shaders/Crosstone.shader\n 635.6 kb     3.6% Assets/Toon/Shader/Toon_ShadingGradeMap_TransClipping.shader\n 618.6 kb     3.5% Assets/Toon/Shader/Toon_ShadingGradeMap.shader\n 7.5 mb     52.4% Assets/_PoiyomiShaders/Shaders/Toon/S_Transparent_PTTO.shader\nTo reproduce, simply create a project with the sdk, and using the aforementioned shaders, doing a build and test vs a build and publish, a discrepancy in avatar file sizes will be found, with shaders sizes being the cause.\nWhile SDK2 does not have a build and test function, the build and publish file sizes seems to match that of SDK3, where all shader variants are included. \nWith regards to SDK2/3 Worlds, it looks like all shader variants are being included as well regardless of test/publish, but I will need to test this more thoroughly.",
